    "chapter_name": "Center of Mass Momentum and Collision",
    "year": "2020",
    "shift": "unknown_shift"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Two bodies of the same mass are connected with an inelastic string of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math>&nbsp;are placed together on a horizontal surface. One of them is projected vertically upwards from the surface with a velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>6</mn><mi>gl</mi></msqrt></math>. The maximum height up to which the centre of mass of the system of the two masses rises is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mtext>l</mtext></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mtext>l</mtext><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mtext>l</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>l</mtext></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0077_bba8a65e845b.jpg\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 113px;\" /><br /><br />The velocity of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;just before the string is taut<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>gl</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>6</mn><mi>gl</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>gl</mi></msqrt><mo>=2</mo><msqrt><mi>gl</mi></msqrt></math><br /><br />After the string is taut, both will move up with same speed, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>mv</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>gl</mi></msqrt></math><br /><br />By this time centre of mass in at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>A further rise in the centre of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>gl</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br />Hence maximum height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math></p>"
  }
